":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eMy company recently provided me a Claude license and even not being a fan of this kind of tool i recognize the value. I think it's great to deal with tasks you don't want to handle and just to get rid of them as fast as possible, but when there is something you like I belive it's importante not to rush it and enjoy the process, for my side projects I don't really allow code generation, instead I try to get the docs and examples on how stuff works then implement it, the risk of atrophy is high and to be able to write good code by yourself is a great value.\nBut I see more and more people convinced I'm not ennjoying the progress, how do you feel about this?\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"My company recently provided me a Claude license and even not being a fan of this kind of tool i recognize the value. I think it's great to deal with tasks you don't want to handle and just to get rid of them as fast as possible, but when there is something you like I belive it's importante not to rush it and enjoy the process, for my side projects I don't really allow code generation, instead I try to get the docs and examples on how stuff works then implement it, the risk of atrophy is high and to be able to write good code by yourself is a great value.\r\nBut I see more and more people convinced I'm not ennjoying the progress, how do you feel about this?","submitter_user":"cedrata","user_is_author":true,"tags":["vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/2eai0v","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/2eai0v/ai_it_s_not_bad_it_s_tool"},{"short_id":"fiirrs","created_at":"2026-09-04T14:46:18.246-05:00","title":"Stop Thinking of LLMs as Next-Token Predictors","url":"https://gmcgoldr.github.io/2026/09/04/llm-next-token-predictors.html","score":6,"flags":1,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"square_usual","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fiirrs","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fiirrs/stop_thinking_llms_as_next_token"},{"short_id":"5iacaa","created_at":"2026-09-04T14:11:37.414-05:00","title":"FLT: Anthropic has beaten me to it","url":"https://xenaproject.wordpress.com/2026/09/04/flt-anthropic-has-beaten-me-to-it/","score":26,"flags":0,"comment_count":5,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"lalitm","user_is_author":false,"tags":["math","vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/5iacaa","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/5iacaa/flt_anthropic_has_beaten_me_it"},{"short_id":"o8bp2s","created_at":"2026-09-04T13:33:44.332-05:00","title":"Babashka 1.13.220 gets FFI","url":"https://blog.michielborkent.nl/babashka-ffi.html","score":18,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"borkdude","user_is_author":true,"tags":["clojure"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/o8bp2s","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/o8bp2s/babashka_1_13_220_gets_ffi"},{"short_id":"rhjedr","created_at":"2026-09-04T12:47:34.388-05:00","title":"jank reimagines C++ errors and gets an official native package repo","url":"https://jank-lang.org/blog/2026-09-04-better-and-better/","score":15,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jeaye","user_is_author":true,"tags":["c++","clojure","compilers","plt"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/rhjedr","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/rhjedr/jank_reimagines_c_errors_gets_official"},{"short_id":"bqfbqk","created_at":"2026-09-04T11:51:46.763-05:00","title":"deft: A gradual type system for Janet","url":"https://codeberg.org/zzkt/deft","score":20,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"e3bc54b2","user_is_author":false,"tags":["lisp"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bqfbqk","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bqfbqk/deft_gradual_type_system_for_janet"},{"short_id":"cywxla","created_at":"2026-09-04T11:20:30.805-05:00","title":"A pr